{
  "info": {
    "name": "HRB Chatbot API",
    "description": "There are only 6 real endpoints. Each top-level folder below is one endpoint; the requests inside it are that endpoint's happy path plus its edge cases, in that order.\n\n1. GET /health — is the service and its backends up\n2. POST /index/v1/rag/documents — upload a PDF\n3. GET /index/v1/rag/documents[/{id}] — list or fetch documents\n4. POST /index/v1/rag/documents/{id}/index — chunk, embed, and index one\n5. POST /search/v1/rag/query — ask a question (stub today, see folder note)\n\nSetup: set `base_url` (local: http://127.0.0.1:8093, or the deployed App Runner URL). Run folder 2's first request once, then copy `results[0].document_id` from the response into the `document_id` variable — folders 3 and 4 need it.\n\nFile uploads (folder 2): the `kb_docs_dir` variable holds the absolute path to resources/kb_docs/ on disk - Postman can't use a relative path there the way curl can, because it has no concept of \"run from the repo root\". Update that one variable if this repo lives somewhere else on your machine. If a file field still shows empty/red after that, click it and re-browse to the PDF by hand - that's a normal Postman re-attach, not a bug.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8093"
    },
    {
      "key": "document_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "kb_docs_dir",
      "value": "C:/workspace/2026-v1/interview-kickstart/hrb_chatbot_v2/resources/kb_docs"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health — GET /health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Shallow (instant, no cost)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Deep, all backends at once",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health?deep=true&provider=anthropic&vector_provider=pinecone&metadata_provider=postgres",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "deep",
                  "value": "true"
                },
                {
                  "key": "provider",
                  "value": "anthropic"
                },
                {
                  "key": "vector_provider",
                  "value": "pinecone"
                },
                {
                  "key": "metadata_provider",
                  "value": "postgres"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "One real, free call per backend - LLM + vector store + metadata store together."
          }
        },
